<Layout title="Vietnam Sourcing & China+1 Supply Chain Strategy | Quick Chan">


<main>


<h1>
Vietnam Sourcing & China+1 Supply Chain Strategy
</h1>


<h2>
Evaluating Alternative Manufacturing Opportunities Across Asia
</h2>


<p class="intro">
A sourcing project supporting supply chain diversification through supplier
research, factory evaluation and manufacturing capability assessment in Vietnam.
</p>



<section>

<h2>
Project Background
</h2>


<p>
A North American client was exploring alternative manufacturing options outside
Mainland China as part of a broader China+1 supply chain diversification strategy.
</p>


<p>
The project focused on evaluating Vietnam's manufacturing capabilities,
supplier availability and production feasibility for future sourcing opportunities.
</p>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Project Scope
</h2>


<ul>

<li>
Supplier identification and market research
</li>

<li>
Factory capability assessment and supplier qualification
</li>

<li>
Manufacturing process and production feasibility evaluation
</li>

<li>
China+1 sourcing strategy support
</li>

</ul>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Challenge
</h2>


<p>
The key challenge was identifying suitable manufacturing partners that could
meet international buyers' expectations while understanding the practical
limitations of Vietnam's manufacturing ecosystem.
</p>


<ul>

<li>
Identifying genuine manufacturers rather than trading companies
</li>

<li>
Assessing supplier production capabilities and available equipment
</li>

<li>
Understanding material availability and manufacturing limitations
</li>

<li>
Evaluating suppliers' experience with international customers
</li>

</ul>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Approach
</h2>


<p>
The sourcing process followed a structured supplier evaluation approach:
</p>


<ul>

<li>
Mapping potential suppliers based on product requirements and manufacturing capabilities
</li>

<li>
Screening factories through capability evaluation and production assessment
</li>

<li>
Reviewing equipment, materials and manufacturing processes
</li>

<li>
Communicating with suppliers to understand commercial feasibility and production suitability
</li>

</ul>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Outcome
</h2>


<p>
The project provided the client with a practical assessment of Vietnam's
manufacturing landscape, including supplier capabilities, production limitations
and potential sourcing opportunities.
</p>


<p>
The findings supported more informed decision-making regarding China+1 supply
chain diversification and future manufacturing strategies.
</p>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Key Takeaway
</h2>


<p>
Successful China+1 sourcing is not simply about finding an alternative supplier.
It requires understanding manufacturing ecosystems, evaluating supplier
capabilities and selecting partners that align with long-term business objectives.
</p>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Confidentiality
</h2>


<p>
Client identities, supplier information and commercial details are protected.
This case study focuses on sourcing methodology, evaluation process and
problem-solving approach rather than confidential business information.
</p>


</section>



